WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:12.559
Hi, everyone.

2
00:00:13.339 --> 00:00:16.300
Our class just finished watching a documentary about the Dead Sea.

3
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.941
We learned a lot of cool stuff about it.

4
00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:23.322
Did you know that people go there just to smear mud all over themselves?

5
00:00:24.242 --> 00:00:25.903
I'll tell you more about that in a minute!

6
00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:30.324
The Dead Sea, in case you don't know, is actually a lake in the Middle East.

7
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.761
At four hundred meters below sea level, it's the lowest point on Earth.

8
00:00:35.581 --> 00:00:39.542
But we found out that it's mostly famous for all the salt and minerals it contains.

9
00:00:40.443 --> 00:00:44.284
The water in the Dead Sea is almost six times saltier than ocean water!

10
00:00:45.564 --> 00:00:49.785
The Dead Sea lies between the borders of Jordan, Israel, and the West Bank.

11
00:00:50.726 --> 00:00:56.487
It's about 80 kilometers long, 11 kilometers wide at its widest point, and 377 meters deep at its

12
00:00:56.527 --> 00:01:05.322
deepest. The lake is surrounded by hot, dry desert on all sides, and it's located in an area

13
00:01:05.422 --> 00:01:07.163
known as the Dead Sea Depression.

14
00:01:08.123 --> 00:01:10.304
I didn't know what a depression was until Mr.

15
00:01:10.364 --> 00:01:14.566
Fay explained that it's a low-lying area caused by something called a rift.

16
00:01:15.487 --> 00:01:18.668
A rift occurs when two plates of the earth's crust move apart.

17
00:01:19.528 --> 00:01:22.069
The land between them gets stretched thinner and thinner.

18
00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.171
And as the land gets thinner, it sinks, creating a depression.

19
00:01:27.552 --> 00:01:31.598
Maybe you're wondering, just like I was, how the Dead Sea got so salty.

20
00:01:32.438 --> 00:01:37.401
Well, the depression sits so low that water from all the nearby rivers drains into it.

21
00:01:38.242 --> 00:01:40.503
This water is filled with salt and minerals.

22
00:01:41.603 --> 00:01:46.646
And since the depression is lower than all the surrounding land, the water can never drain back out;

23
00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.107
it can only evaporate.

24
00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.889
And that's what happens—water constantly evaporates.

25
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:58.085
In fact, so much water is evaporating from the Dead Sea, it often looks like there's a cloud

26
00:01:58.105 --> 00:01:59.626
of fog hanging over the lake.

27
00:01:59.646 --> 00:02:03.628
(That's pretty creepy when you think about the Dead Sea's name, huh?)

28
00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:08.691
Anyway, as the water evaporates, it leaves behind the salt and minerals.

29
00:02:10.192 --> 00:02:13.894
Now I can tell you why people go to the Dead Sea to cover themselves from head to

30
00:02:14.014 --> 00:02:15.195
toe with its mud!

31
00:02:16.095 --> 00:02:20.218
All the minerals that get deposited into the lake sink down into the mud at the bottom.

32
00:02:21.098 --> 00:02:23.820
And those minerals are supposed to be really good for your skin.

33
00:02:24.712 --> 00:02:27.794
No wonder lots of spas and health resorts have been built in the area.

34
00:02:28.674 --> 00:02:33.176
After hearing so much about the Dead Sea's health benefits, I wanted to know why it has such

35
00:02:33.216 --> 00:02:34.096
a grim name.

36
00:02:34.997 --> 00:02:40.079
According to the documentary we watched in class, the water in the Dead Sea is so salty that

37
00:02:40.179 --> 00:02:44.181
almost nothing can live there, except for bacteria and one type of algae.

38
00:02:45.742 --> 00:02:50.364
Any fish or freshwater animal that gets washed into the lake dies almost instantly.

39
00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:56.846
And the shores are covered in thick salt crystals, so animals can't even survive near the lake either.

40
00:02:57.727 --> 00:03:00.548
But don't worry; the water is totally safe for people.

41
00:03:01.368 --> 00:03:06.070
You can even go swimming there if you want, although it's pretty hard to swim because all that

42
00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:08.031
salt makes it much easier to float!

43
00:03:09.071 --> 00:03:13.593
In fact, that movie showed people sitting up and reading in the Dead Sea, as if they were

44
00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:14.493
sitting in chairs.

45
00:03:15.474 --> 00:03:16.874
It was unbelievable!

46
00:03:18.355 --> 00:03:20.676
The Dead Sea also has an important place in history.

47
00:03:21.524 --> 00:03:26.207
It's mentioned in the Bible, and there are stories about Queen Cleopatra traveling to the lake to bathe.

48
00:03:27.248 --> 00:03:29.429
It's also where the Dead Sea Scrolls were discovered.

49
00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:37.114
These ancient manuscripts, which were made from papyrus, leather, and copper, were found in 1947 in caves near

50
00:03:37.134 --> 00:03:37.875
the lake's shore.

51
00:03:38.736 --> 00:03:43.539
They're the oldest known copies of the Old Testament, dating all the way back to the third and

52
00:03:43.619 --> 00:03:45.180
first centuries BC.

53
00:03:46.108 --> 00:03:51.894
Unfortunately, like many other beautiful and historic places in the world, the Dead Sea's existence is threatened.

54
00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:57.739
Over the last thirty years or so, its water level has dropped by nearly one meter a year,

55
00:03:58.119 --> 00:04:00.982
and it has lost almost a third of its surface area.

56
00:04:02.383 --> 00:04:06.928
This is because the waters of its main source—the Jordan River—are being diverted.

57
00:04:07.796 --> 00:04:13.420
The countries of Israel, Syria, and Jordan are diverting fresh water from the Jordan River in order to

58
00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.402
farm and provide drinking water to people living in cities.

59
00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:23.367
Israel and Jordan also deliberately evaporate large pools of water just to extract the Dead Sea's minerals.

60
00:04:24.288 --> 00:04:27.811
The scientists in the movie think the depression itself is sinking every year too.

61
00:04:28.771 --> 00:04:30.973
Some scientists think the rift is the cause.

62
00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:35.216
Others believe that the sinking is due to changes in the ground's composition.

63
00:04:36.156 --> 00:04:40.678
Either way the lake is reported to sink about 33 centimeters every year!

64
00:04:42.079 --> 00:04:43.059
Sadly Mr.

65
00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:47.221
Fay said that the countries around the Dead Sea don't have the greatest relations right now.

66
00:04:48.101 --> 00:04:53.063
That makes it very difficult for environmentalists to come together and try to help the Jordan River and

67
00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:53.784
the Dead Sea.

68
00:04:54.644 --> 00:04:55.684
But I hope they do.

69
00:04:56.605 --> 00:04:58.465
I want to try floating there someday!

70
00:04:59.306 --> 00:05:03.448
After we watched the movie about the Dead Sea, Alex and I came up with a great idea

71
00:05:03.488 --> 00:05:09.234
for a project: our class can write letters to environmental protection groups asking them to support the conservation

72
00:05:09.254 --> 00:05:10.076
of the Jordan River.

73
00:05:10.897 --> 00:05:13.300
This will help to save the "dying" Dead Sea.

74
00:05:14.181 --> 00:05:16.825
The movie definitely gave me a lot of facts for my letter.

75
00:05:17.626 --> 00:05:20.529
But I still have more research to do, so I'd better go now.

76
00:05:21.451 --> 00:05:22.172
See you next time!
